## Resuming in a new session (lead)

Work spans many sessions; reconstruct state from durable sources, not chat history. On start:
1. Read this file and `docs/decisions.md` (the why behind the setup).
2. `gh issue list --state open` (the queue) · `gh pr list` (in review) · `git log --oneline -12`.
3. Identify the current phase (`docs/roadmap.md`, if this project uses one) and the next
   unblocked issue.
Or run `/harness:project-status` for an automated snapshot. Durable state = GitHub
issues/PRs + `docs/decisions.md` + this file — keep them current as decisions change.
The write-side is `/harness:checkpoint`: run it at wave boundaries (post-merge, before a
new workstream, or when the session is getting heavy) — don't wait to be asked.
